1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,493
Start in TV Quotes, under Build and estimate.

2
00:00:03,493 --> 00:00:07,815
The workspace keeps your equipment, selling price
and purchase order together.

3
00:00:07,815 --> 00:00:09,779
This is a training example.

4
00:00:09,779 --> 00:00:15,672
Open Client and terms to enter the client, delivery
location, quote expiry and lead time.

5
00:00:15,672 --> 00:00:19,994
Linking an existing deal can fill in the available
client details.

6
00:00:21,094 --> 00:00:24,213
Choose Add TV to browse the display catalog.

7
00:00:24,213 --> 00:00:29,280
Search a model, narrow the screen size, or compare
up to three choices.

8
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:31,619
The pictures represent each product series.

9
00:00:31,619 --> 00:00:34,348
Choose a display, then enter the quantity.

10
00:00:34,348 --> 00:00:37,077
Expand its details to assign a location.

11
00:00:37,077 --> 00:00:41,365
Unit cost, margin and selling price remain visible
beside the line.

12
00:00:42,465 --> 00:00:45,433
Add the mounts and services the job needs.

13
00:00:45,433 --> 00:00:50,999
Enter their quantities and costs, and check which
lines belong on the vendor purchase order.

14
00:00:50,999 --> 00:00:54,338
The totals stay at the bottom while you work.

15
00:00:54,338 --> 00:00:57,677
For repeated installations, save this equipment as a
package.

16
00:00:57,677 --> 00:01:01,016
Apply it at another location with a quantity
multiplier.

17
00:01:01,016 --> 00:01:03,613
Paste from Excel adds several rows together.

18
00:01:03,613 --> 00:01:06,210
Review the quantities and prices before continuing.

19
00:01:08,283 --> 00:01:10,924
Review and export opens the client preview.

20
00:01:10,924 --> 00:01:13,566
Check the equipment, quantities, terms and total.

21
00:01:13,566 --> 00:01:18,471
The internal workbook contains the quote, cost and
margin, and purchase order sheets.

22
00:01:18,471 --> 00:01:22,621
Prepare client document creates the proposal for PDF
or Word export.

23
00:01:22,621 --> 00:01:24,885
Preparing it does not send it.

24
00:01:24,885 --> 00:01:28,659
Mark it sent only after sharing it with the client.

25
00:01:30,115 --> 00:01:35,179
Open Purchasing and check the vendor, requester,
delivery address and payment terms.

26
00:01:35,179 --> 00:01:40,243
Issue purchase order assigns a number and saves the
equipment at cost.

27
00:01:40,243 --> 00:01:45,307
The issued PDF keeps those quantities, even when the
quote changes later.

28
00:01:45,307 --> 00:01:47,839
Here, we increase the display quantity.

29
00:01:47,839 --> 00:01:51,215
The workspace flags that the equipment has changed.

30
00:01:51,215 --> 00:01:55,013
Issue a new revision when those changes are ready.

31
00:01:55,013 --> 00:02:00,078
The order keeps its number, and the earlier revision
remains in history.

32
00:02:01,178 --> 00:02:05,225
Quote history keeps the issued purchase order
revisions available to download.

33
00:02:05,225 --> 00:02:09,272
With a linked deal, Purchasing shows whether the CRM
update succeeded

34
00:02:09,272 --> 00:02:11,480
and provides a retry when needed.

35
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:14,423
Before leaving, check that the quote says Saved.

36
00:02:14,423 --> 00:02:18,102
If a save fails, your draft stays in the editor

37
00:02:18,102 --> 00:02:20,310
and exports wait until saving succeeds.

38
00:02:20,310 --> 00:02:22,885
Review the final documents before sending them.
